      "writtenOn": "2021-12-28T23:02:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you elaborate why this change is needed -- as a refactoring it\u0027s not very useful as it makes the code longer, not shorter, and it does not appear that there will be more functions that might leverage this change.",
      "revId": "458d1187c6b43931bce33144c5467e4bc7343f0d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d75f1ee3_aed20fbe",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-28T23:13:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because it makes the code easier to understand. Here are some examples:\n\n1. ParseReference now always returns a valid expression or a badExpression, when previously it could return invalid call expressions that had to be handled separately.\n2. Functions that require special parsing are now handled the same way as other functions, instead of requiring to add more special handling code in parseReference or parseCompareSpecialCases.\n3. Special cases are no longer encoded in strings with an !\n4. There are now no functions in knownFunctions that we can\u0027t convert.\n\nAs for more functions that might leverage this change, I was planning on using this to add support for math_gt_or_eq, as that would require custom code to put the casts to int and \u003e\u003d literals into the starlark.",
      "parentUuid": "a1463317_050d770a",
      "revId": "458d1187c6b43931bce33144c5467e4bc7343f0d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6e4f1b4_d2faa42a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-28T23:15:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also it doesn\u0027t really make the code any longer. It\u0027s ~20 lines longer in the diff, but that\u0027s only because I added a new globalsExpr. I could replace that with identifierExpr if you want, and then the diff will have similar line counts before/after. I just thought the globalsExpr was meaningful.",
      "parentUuid": "d75f1ee3_aed20fbe",
      "revId": "458d1187c6b43931bce33144c5467e4bc7343f0d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7277329b_e7351f5d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1344584
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-29T04:29:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Overall this fairly large change seems to be replacing a switch statement with dispatch. It\u0027s unclear to me why this is a better way to handle it, it\u0027s still case-by-case handling.\nIf you insist on this, I\u0027d suggest to introduce an interface, say, funcCallParser with a single method parse(), and then implement this interface for simpleFuncCall, wildcardCall, shellCall, ... types. The knownFunctions then can map function\u0027s name to the corresponding parser type object rather than a function factory.\nAs to your math_gt_or_eq example, sure, it\u0027s needed, but I don\u0027t see how this change will make it easier.",
      "parentUuid": "b6e4f1b4_d2faa42a",
      "revId": "458d1187c6b43931bce33144c5467e4bc7343f0d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
