      "writtenOn": "2022-01-04T19:29:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct, a struct type for each specific parser, and funcCallParser.parse() will have parseContext as its first argument. A struct allows to keep the needed context in an IMHO more natural way, so instead of parseSimpleCallFactory you have \ntype simpleFuncCall struct {\n  name string\n  returnType ...\n  addGlobals bool\n}\nand knownFunctions can be initialized statically.",
      "parentUuid": "3f00d76d_b2653c7f",
      "revId": "458d1187c6b43931bce33144c5467e4bc7343f0d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
